THOUGHT: The checks are substantial, but the core can be implemented efficiently with a single shared SQLite database and three HTTP listeners using Python’s standard library. I’ll now create the initial service with authentication, workspaces, channels, roles, messages, pagination, reactions, pins, reads, search, a basic SPA, and WebSocket support, then run the regression suite to expose gaps.

```mswea_bash_command
cat > /app/server.py <<'PY'
import os, re, json, sqlite3, hashlib, secrets, threading, time, base64, struct, socket, socketserver
from http.server import ThreadingHTTPServer, BaseHTTPRequestHandler
from urllib.parse import urlparse, parse_qs
from datetime import datetime, timezone

DB='/app/chat.db'
LOCK=threading.RLock()
def now(): return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec='milliseconds').replace('+00:00','Z')
def conn():
    c=sqlite3.connect(DB,check_same_thread=False); c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row; return c
def init():
    c=conn()
    c.executescript('''
    PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL;
    CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,username TEXT UNIQUE,password TEXT,display_name TEXT,timezone TEXT DEFAULT 'UTC',avatar_url TEXT DEFAULT '',status_text TEXT DEFAULT '',status_emoji TEXT DEFAULT '');
    CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tokens(token TEXT PRIMARY KEY,user_id INTEGER);
